it can be hard to tell where Bangladesh  ends and India begins that stone marks  the divide put a foot wrong and it could  cost you your life  ma feasel Rahman was found dead early on  January 21st he had a single bullet  wound to his chest his mud-caked feet a  typical of someone who's been working in  a rice paddy two days later at dawn  Kamal Haasan went to tend the paddies  later that day his body was brought back  to his family  wrapped in a shroud he was brutally  killed by the Indian border guards we  want justice for this he was the only  breadwinner now he's dead we're totally  helpless now how are we going to manage  by the end of January in just one month  the Indian border forces had killed 15  Bangladeshis over the past 20 years more  than a thousand people have been killed  according to Human Rights Watch we don't  want any more killings in the border  they can arrest and can punish the  people jail them or find them but  instead they're shooting them dead  sometimes the Indians will take people  just for crossing a few centimeters in  to the other side by mistake and to  detain them for years we want some fair  justice and a peaceful border this is  our request to the government this is  India's border fence but as is the  practice internationally it's set back  from the actual boundary line it's in  the Indian Territory between the fence  and the markers that the shootings  happen now it's this easy to stray from  Bangladesh into India you can just about  make out India carved in the stone there  now the Indian authorities have  repeatedly promised to bring the number  of border killings down to zero and to  introduce non-lethal weapons but it's  clearly not happening the Indian  government has said it's fighting  illegal cross-border cattle trading al  Jazeera did not receive a response from  the government to our questions about  the killings  none of those killed in January was  found with lethal weapons  buzz Nattie Ronnie's son Sansa was also  shot dead last month he could have been  punished or jailed instead she says  Bangladeshis home minister said this  week he's taking necessary measures at a  diplomatic level to stop the killings  similar comments have been made several  times over the past years but India's  border guards are still opening fire  Burnett Smith al Jazeera on the  Bangladesh India border
 

